## UX Improvements Implementation

I've implemented two UX improvements to enhance the visual feedback for player actions:

### 1. JUMP Visual Indicator Positioning
- Fixed the JUMP visual indicator to appear underneath the avatar by its feet instead of in the middle
- Added special handling for both geometric shapes and 3D man avatars
- For geometric shapes, the indicator appears below the bottom edge with a small gap
- For Guy models (3D man avatars), the indicator is positioned at the feet level
- Increased the JUMP text size by 25% for better visibility
- Made the JUMP indicator 25% larger overall

### 2. Double-Tap Direction Key Visual Feedback
- Implemented a double-tap detection system for left and right arrow keys
- When a player double-taps a direction key within 300ms, a "RUN" text appears to the side of the avatar
- Added a trail effect that shows particles behind the avatar when running
- The trail consists of fading, colored particles that match the player's color
- Both the text and trail animate and fade out over time
- Made the RUN indicator 25% larger for better visibility
- Positioned the RUN indicator to the side of the avatar instead of above it

### 3. Player Name Labels
- Fixed issue where player names weren't appearing on top of avatars
- Created a dedicated label group structure to ensure names are always visible
- Positioned player name labels well above the avatar's head
- Set high renderOrder value (999) to ensure labels are rendered on top of other elements
- Increased the size of player name labels for better visibility
- Ensured player names are always visible and not replaced by indicators
- Used a separate group structure for indicators to prevent them from interfering with name labels
- Made player names 25% larger and more prominent
- Updated the name update logic to maintain proper positioning when names change

These visual improvements provide better feedback to players about their actions, making the game more intuitive and visually engaging, while ensuring important information like player names remains clearly visible at all times.

