## Player Name Label Fix

I've implemented a comprehensive fix for the player name labels to ensure they always appear on top of the avatars:

### 1. Enhanced Player Label Visibility
- Modified the player label sprites to use `depthTest: false` and `depthWrite: false` to ensure they always render on top
- Set `sizeAttenuation: false` so the labels don't get smaller with distance
- Increased the label size significantly (scale 3.0, 0.8, 1)
- Set an extremely high renderOrder (9999) to ensure labels are drawn last

### 2. Improved Label Positioning
- Positioned labels much higher above the avatar's head (1.2x avatar height)
- Created a dedicated label group with special userData flags for identification
- Added proper reference tracking between labels and avatars

### 3. Continuous Label Monitoring
- Added a new `updatePlayerLabels()` function that runs every frame in the animation loop
- This function ensures all player labels maintain their visibility settings
- Checks and corrects label positions if they're not properly above the avatar
- Handles edge cases where labels might be incorrectly positioned

These changes ensure that player names are always clearly visible on top of avatars, regardless of camera angle or other scene elements.

