## Crush Action Trail Effect Fix

I've modified the crush/arrow down trail effect to only trigger once when the crush action is activated:

### 1. Added Crush Action Tracking
- Created a new `crushActionTracking` object to track the state of the crush action
- Added properties to track if the effect is currently active and when it was last activated
- Implemented a 500ms cooldown period between crush effects

### 2. Modified Arrow Down Event Handler
- Updated the keydown handler to check if the crush effect is already active
- Only creates the trail effect if not active and the cooldown period has passed
- Sets the crush action as active and records the activation time
- Uses setTimeout to automatically reset the active state after the animation completes

### 3. Added Arrow Down Key Release Handler
- Added a keyup handler specifically for the arrow down key
- Ensures the crush action tracking is properly reset when the key is released
- Acts as a safety measure in case the setTimeout in keydown fails

These changes ensure the crush trail effect only triggers once per crush action activation, preventing multiple overlapping effects when the key is held down.

